Gate: SECRETS

Purpose:
  Secret detection — ensure no secrets, credentials, or sensitive
  data are hardcoded or committed to version control.

AppliesTo:
  - Source code
  - Configuration files
  - Environment files
  - Documentation
  - Build artifacts

When:
  - All code changes
  - Pre-commit
  - Pre-merge
  - CI/CD pipeline

Tools:
  - Gitleaks
  - TruffleHog
  - GitGuardian
  - detect-secrets
  - custom regex patterns

MustPass:
  - No hardcoded API keys
  - No hardcoded passwords
  - No hardcoded private keys
  - No hardcoded tokens
  - No hardcoded database credentials
  - No hardcoded cloud credentials
  - No exposed OAuth secrets

MayPass:
  - Test/example secrets with explicit approval
  - Placeholder values (e.g., YOUR_API_KEY_HERE)

Block:
  - Any hardcoded secret with real value
  - Any credential in source code
  - Any private key in repository
  - Any token in logs or configs

OnFail:
  - Finding created immediately
  - Secret MUST be rotated
  - Task created for remediation
  - Chain BLOCKED until secret rotated and verified

Exceptions:
  - Test fixtures MAY contain fake secrets
  - Documentation MAY contain example values (must be clearly marked as examples)

State: +
  
